#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Validate the merge gate's policy: policy/risk.yml, policy/autonomy.json and policy/risk-cases.json.

  bin/check-policy [--dir POLICY_DIR]
      Exit 0: the three files are valid and every case gets its class, flags and level.
      Exit 1: one line per problem, each naming its file and rule. Exit 2: usage.

risk.yml says which class (R0-R3) a PR is; autonomy.json says who may merge which class in which
repo (L0-L4); risk-cases.json holds the cases every implementation of the rule must pass (hq#210's
gate in sk-ctl runs the same file). risk.yml is written as JSON, which YAML 1.2 also reads, so no
YAML parser is needed anywhere. The reference matcher below is decision 0006's (hq
tools/merge_gate/tiered_merge.py at de93ba3): glob_re, denied and category are ports of it.

Python 3 standard library only, like bin/dependabot-policy, so it runs on the agent VMs and the
runners. The floors at the top are copies from hq de93ba3: the policy files may add to them, never
drop from them. A floor changes only with a change to this file.
"""
import fnmatch
import json
import os
import re
import sys

